  "jp": "胴付き蟻継ぎ",
  "gloss": "",
  "guidance": "A dovetail cut in plan rather than in elevation: the tenon is 60 mm wide at the shoulders and 100 mm at the nose, so once B is lowered over it the two timbers cannot be pulled apart along their length. The socket runs the full 120 mm depth, which is what lets B drop straight down onto the tenon while the shoulders at the seam meet.",
